		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5127&amp;p=37137#p37137"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>How do upgrade the firmware without the opengd77 CPS?<br>How do I backup the original firmware?<br><br>The instructions that I read indicated the radio must be in DFU mode. <br><br>I must me looking in the wrong spot<br><br>Thanks <br>            Phil NC3S</div></blockquote><br>It is not possible to backup the original firmware in the radio. But you can backup the flash memory after installing OpenGD77 <br><br>DFU stands for Device Firmware Upgrade, and the radio must be in this mode to update the firmware<br><br>You can only install OpenGD77 using the CPS on Windows, or using the Python script on Linux.  ( I can't remember if the python script works on Windows)<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri May 16, 2025 8:40 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
