		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5127&amp;p=37134#p37134"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello,<br><br>This is my first post, so I hope the question is understandable.<br><br>My PC is running Windows 11 Pro.<br><br>I have a Retevis RT3S (gps) that I want to install opengd77 on.<br><br>Currently I have the Retevis supplied CPS working correctly with no issues.<br><br>When I try to use opengd77 CPS, no serial port is created in my Device Manager listing.<br><br>I have 5 other radio related ports that currently exist, for HF radios.<br><br>Opendg77 CPS wants me to select a port, but none exist for it.  I'm not sure what is going on since the Retevis supplied CPS works as expected, it never asks for a port.<br><br>I'm don't know were to go from here.<br><br>BTW: the radio was in DFU mode (PTT + SK1)<br><br>Thanks,<br>      Phil, NC3S</div></blockquote>You can't read or write config to the radio with OpenGD77 CPS when the radio is running factory firmware, radio must have OpenGD77 running  to appear as a COM port in device manager.<br><br>DFU mode is used for firmware updates and when radio is started in DFU mode (flashing red/green led) you should see the radio under <br>"Universal Serial Bus controllers"<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2979&amp;sid=cf17a0dd594a0677cc7a32e01560ea73" class="postimage" alt="STM_driver_in_DFU_mode.JPG" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Fri May 16, 2025 5:59 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
